methods.differs_from:
- OGD (Farajtabar 2020) uses the same null space of output gradients. But it stores the gradients of about 200 fixed samples, uses SGD, and is supervised. FN-PPO instead:
  - refreshes anchors from simulation banks at the current weights every PPO iteration;
  - projects Adam's output step;
  - gets the exact Gram matrix of all trunk-Jacobian rows from (G G^T) ⊙ (Z Z^T + 1) without materialising them;
  - adds a Gauss-Newton restore step;
  - runs in multi-head stage-extension RL with an exploration floor.
- GPM, Adam-NSCL and SGP block the old INPUT subspace, which holds 94-97% of our new skill's energy; the prediction is about head-only speed (3.1M). FN-PPO blocks only what changes old OUTPUTS, so old features remain usable as inputs.
- KL/BC replay (Wolczyk 2024, ClonEx, ACCRUE) is the soft penalty. It needs a λ trade-off, and Adam's normalisation dilutes the PPO gradient once the penalty dominates. FN-PPO is the λ → ∞ limit without that stiffness.
- CHAIN (Tang & Berseth 2024) penalises output churn on a reference batch, but within a single task.
- EWC uses a diagonal Fisher; FN-PPO uses the exact function-space Jacobian.
- The novelty is the RL recipe and its evidence, not the linear algebra.
